          "type": "PARALLEL"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Consolidate Exceptions"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "CONSOLIDATE_EXCEPTIONS",
          "id": "1762510080548",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1762510080550_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$variables.llmPersona}}\nPayroll diagnostic outputs:\n1. {{$context.$nodes.E1_TERM_HIRE_REASON.$output}}\n\n2. {{$context.$nodes.E2_ASG_ATTR_CHANGES_REASON.$output}} \n\n3. {{$context.$nodes.E3_SALARY_CHANGES_REASON.$output}} \n\n4.  {{$context.$nodes.E4_RETRO_EVENTS_REASON.$output}} \n\n5.  {{$context.$nodes.E5_PAYRELHISTORY_REASON.$output}}\n\n6.  {{$context.$nodes.E6_EEHISTORY_REASON.$output}} \n\n7. {{$context.$nodes.E7_NETPAYS_REASON.$output}} \n\n8. {{$context.$nodes.E8_COSTING_REASON.$output}} \n\n9. {{$context.$nodes.E9_ARREARS_NT_REASON.$output}} \n\n10. {{$context.$nodes.E10_TRU_REASON.$output}} \n\nFrom the above payroll diagnostic output, return only the reported payroll exceptions as an HTML unordered list (<ul><li>...</li></ul>).\n\nWhen multiple issues clearly reference the same underlying record or object (even if described using different labels), group them together under a neutral parent label.\n\nWhen multiple issues share a common attribute, represent the shared attribute as a parent list item, and list the individual issues under it using a nested <ul>. Nest further only when an additional shared attribute is clearly stated in the data. When numeric values or balances are explicitly reported as part of the same described condition, they may be nested under that condition as supporting details, without stating or implying causality. Each lowest-level list item must describe exactly one concrete reported change or condition, using a single concise sentence.\n\nGroup all reported changes first by their explicit functional area (e.g., “Element Entries”).\nWithin each functional area, group by clearly shared underlying records such as the same “AssignmentId\", \"AssignmentNumber”, “PayrollRelationshipNumber”, “Element”, or any other explicitly stated common identifier.\nNest further only when an additional shared attribute is clearly present in the data.\nDo not infer relationships, and ensure each lowest-level item describes exactly one concrete change including all identifiers and values exactly as provided.\n\nDo not prefix any list item with words like \"Exception\" or \"Exception due to\".\n\nDo not infer, assume, or invent relationships that are not explicitly stated.\n\nExclude all ids, deeplinks, headings, system messages, follow-up questions, and any entries or text that merely state the absence of exceptions.\n\nDo not mention node names in output.\n\nDo not omit, summarize, generalize, or drop any data fields present in the input. Every reported change must explicitly include all contextual identifiers and labels exactly as provided in the source data (including record numbers, element names, and value names). Treat these identifiers as mandatory output content, not optional metadata. Any response that excludes such data is considered incomplete.\n\nIf no reported exceptions exist, return exactly:\nNo exceptions found for this person."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "E1 TermHire Reason"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1762510080548"
          },
          "code": "E1_TERM_HIRE_REASON",
          "id": "1762935667076",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1762935667081_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$variables.llmPersona}} \n\n# Payroll Relationship Data\n {{$context.$nodes.E1_GET_PAYROLL_RELATIONSHIP.$output}}\n\n\n# Payroll Period Start Date: {{$context.$nodes.GET_VALIDATION_DATES.$output.EarnStartDate}}\n# Payroll Period End Date:  {{$context.$nodes.GET_VALIDATION_DATES.$output.EarnEndDate}}\n\n\n# Exception Logic:\nExamine the First Standard Earning Date and the Last Standard Earning Date for the payroll calculation.  \n    If the First Standard Earning Date is after the payroll period start date and before the payroll period end date, but not equal to the payroll period start date, mark this as an exception.  \n    If the Last Standard Earning Date is after the payroll period start date and before the payroll period end date, but not equal to the payroll period end date, also mark this as an exception.  \n    If neither condition applies, do not mark it as an exception.\n\n# Exception Reporting format:\n If an exception is found, begin the output with: \"There is an exception due to first earning date or last earning date in the middle of this payroll period\"\n    Then, display the First Standard Earning Date and/or Last Standard Earning Date that triggered the exception.  \nIf no exception is found, output: \"No exception due to first standard earning or last standard earning date in this payroll calculation.\" \n\n{{$context.$variables.llmSysPrompt}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
