        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "E5 PayRelHistory Reason"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1762510080548"
          },
          "code": "E5_PAYRELHISTORY_REASON",
          "id": "1763367388572",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1763367388573_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$variables.llmPersona}} \n\n# Payroll Relationship History data\n{{$context.$nodes.E5_GET_PAY_REL_HISTORY.$output}} \n\n# Payroll Period Start Date: {{$context.$nodes.GET_VALIDATION_DATES.$output.EarnStartDate}}\n# Payroll Period End Date:  {{$context.$nodes.GET_VALIDATION_DATES.$output.EarnEndDate}}\n\n# Exception Logic:\n\nData Preparation:\n\nFrom the given assigned payroll history, payroll assignment history data and specified payroll period (between start and end dates), filter the data based on these rules:\n\nFor Assigned Payroll History:\n\n1) Consider any records where the value has changed within the payroll period.\n2) Consider any new records where the effective start date is not same as the payroll period start date but exists between the payroll period start and end date, and the effective end date is neither the payroll period end date nor extend beyond the payroll period end date.\n3) Do not consider records where both the effective start date and effective end date are outside of the payroll period.\n\nSorting:\nSort the remaining data sets by Effective Start Date in ascending order. \n\nComparison:\nFor each pair of consecutive data sets (from the above filtered data), compare the following attributes: Time Card Required and Overtime Period.     \n\nTreat a null value as \"no value assigned\" for comparison purposes.\n\nIf both data sets have null or same value for the same attribute, skip the comparison for that attribute.\n\nIf a difference is found in any attribute between the two data sets, mark this as an exception.\n\nSingle Record Exception:\nIf there is exactly one record within the period after filtering, and either its Effective Start Date OR Effective End Date falls within the payroll period but effective start date is not same as payroll period start date and  effective end date is not same as payroll period end date, report it as an exception.\n\nPayroll Assignment History:   \nPerform the same comparison (as above) and for each assignment's data sets for the same two attributes from payroll assignment data set. Mark the exception or no exception using the same logic as mentioned above.\n\nRepeat this process for each assignment.\n\nIf no differences are found in either assigned payroll or payroll assignment data sets using the above logic, then do not mark it as an exception.\n\n# Exception Reporting format:\n\nIf an exception is found in assigned payroll, output:\n    \"There is an exception due to assigned payroll changes in this payroll period.\"\n\nFor each change, output:\nPayroll Name: <Payroll Name>\n  Then, for each changed attribute, show: <Attribute Name>: <previous value> changed to <new value> as of <new value effective start date>.\n\nFor Single Entry exceptions in Assigned Payroll, output:\n\nThere is an exception for the assigned payroll within the payroll period, which may impact the payroll calculation.\n\nPayroll: \"<Payroll Name>\"\nTimecard Required: \"<Timecard Required>\"\nOvertime Period: \"<Overtime Period>\"\nEffective Start Date: \"<Effective Start Date>\"\nEffective End Date: \"<Effective End Date>\"\n\nIf an exception is found in payroll assignment, group the results by Assignment Number, and output:\n    \"There is an exception due to payroll assignment changes in this payroll period.\"\n   Then, for each changed attribute, show: <Attribute Name>: <previous value> changed to <new value> as of <new value effective start date>.\n    Repeat for each affected assignment. \n\nFor Single Entry exceptions in payroll assignment, output:\n\nThere is an exception in the payroll assignment within the payroll period, which may impact the payroll calculation.\n\nAssignment: \"<Assignment Number>\"\nTimecard Required: \"<Timecard Required>\"\nOvertime Period: \"<Overtime Period>\"\nEffective Start Date: \"<Effective Start Date>\"\nEffective End Date: \"<Effective End Date>\"\n\nIf no exceptions are detected in both assigned payroll and payroll assignment data sets, output: \"No exception due to assigned payroll or payroll assignment changes.\"\n\n{{$context.$variables.llmSysPrompt}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
