        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "E6 EEHistory Reason"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1762510080548"
          },
          "code": "E6_EEHISTORY_REASON",
          "id": "1763369595195",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1763369595197_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$variables.llmPersona}} \n\nSummarize the provided JSON change data into a concise, structured report.\n\nInput:\n {{$context.$nodes.E6_PRE_REASON.$output.result}}\n\nOutput requirements:\n1) Group changes first by AssignmentChanges (AssignmentId) and PayrollRelationshipChanges (PayrollRelationshipNumber).\n2) Within each assignment/payroll relationship, group by ElementName.\n3) For each element, list InputValueName changes with AsOfDate and value transitions, omit if not present.\n4) Keep the output concise but complete, and ensure no changes are omitted.\n\nOutput format (example structure):\nRecurring Element Entry Changes\n- AssignmentChanges (skip if empty)\n  - AssignmentId: <number>\n    - Element entry for element: <ElementName>\n      - <InputValueName>: <created/updated/deleted> (in case of updates : from: <FromValue>, to: <ToValue> )  as of date: <date>\n- PayrollRelationshipChanges (skip if empty)\n  - PayrollRelationshipNumber: <number>\n    - Element entry for element: <ElementName>\n      - <InputValueName>: <created/updated/deleted> (in case of updates : from: <FromValue>, to: <ToValue> )  as of date: <date>\n\nNow produce the summary for the given JSON.\n     \n\n    No exceptions: \n    If no differences are found, output exactly:\n    No exception due to recurring entry changes in this payroll calculation\n\n{{$context.$variables.llmSysPrompt}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "E7 NetPays Reason"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1762510080548"
          },
          "code": "E7_NETPAYS_REASON",
          "id": "1763373181473",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1763373181475_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$variables.llmPersona}} \n\n# Statement of earnings data:\n {{$context.$nodes.E7_FOR_EACH_OBJACTION.$output}}\n\n# Exception Logic\n\nCollect all entries from all datasets (or payroll runs) where BalanceName = \"Net Payment\" for the given payroll period and person.\n     Count the number of \"Net Payment\" entries.\n     If the total number of \"Net Payment\" entries is not exactly one, OR if any \"Net Payment\" Value1 is zero (including cases where all are zero):\n        Report an exception.\n         \n     If exactly one \"Net Payment\" entry exists and its Value1 is not zero:\n        Do not report an exception.\n\n# Exception Reporting Format\nIf an exception is found:\nThere is an exception due to multiple net payments for this person in this payroll period.\nList of Net Payment balances found:\n\n- Net Payment 1: <currency> <amount1> \n- Net Payment 2: <currency> <amount2>\n...\nSum of all net payment balances: <currency> <sum>\n\n\nIf no exception is found, output: \"No exceptions due to multiple payroll calculations for this person in this payroll period.\"\n\nDo NOT emit any exception text if the Net Payment count does not exceed one.\n\n{{$context.$variables.llmSysPrompt}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
