        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "E10 TRU Reason"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1762510080548"
          },
          "code": "E10_TRU_REASON",
          "id": "1764923919969",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1764923919971_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$variables.llmPersona}} \n\n# Payroll Calculation Entries History data\n {{$context.$nodes.E10_GET_CALC_HISTORY.$output}}.\n\n# Payroll Period Start Date: {{$context.$nodes.GET_VALIDATION_DATES.$output.EarnStartDate}}\n# Payroll Period End Date:  {{$context.$nodes.GET_VALIDATION_DATES.$output.EarnEndDate}}\n\n# Exception Logic:\n\nData Preparation:\n\nGiven above data and specified payroll period (between start and end dates), filter the data based on these rules:\n\n1) Consider any records where the value has changed within the payroll period.\n2) Consider any new records where the effective start date is not same as the payroll period start date but exists between the payroll period start and end date, and the effective end date is neither the payroll period end date nor extend beyond the payroll period end date.\n3) Do not consider records where both the effective start date and effective end date are outside of the payroll period.\n\nSorting:\nSort the remaining data sets by Effective Start Date in ascending order. \n\nComparison:\nFor each pair of consecutive data sets (from the above filtered data), compare the following attributes: Tax Reporting Unit.     \n\nTreat a null value as \"no value assigned\" for comparison purposes.\n\nIf both data sets have null or same value for the same attribute, skip the comparison for that attribute.\n\nIf a difference is found in any attribute between the two data sets, mark this as an exception for that assignment.\n\nRepeat this process for each assignment.\n\nSingle Record Exception:\nIf there is exactly one record within the period after filtering, and either its Effective Start Date OR Effective End Date falls within the payroll period but effective start date is not same as payroll period start date and  effective end date is not same as payroll period end date, report it as an exception.\n\nIf no differences are found related to tax reporting unit between consecutive data sets, then do not mark it as an exception.\n\n\n\n# Exception Reporting format:\n\nIf an exception is found:\nThere is an exception due to tax reporting unit changes in this payroll period.\n\nGroup the data by Assignment Number.\n    For each change, output:\nAssignment Number: <Assignment Number>\n  Then, for each changed attribute, show: <Attribute Name>: <previous value> changed to <new value> as of <new value effective start date>.\n\nRepeat this for each assignment.\n\nFor Single Record Exception, output:\n\nThere is an exception due to tax reporting unit changes in the payroll period that may impact the payroll calculation.\nAssignment: \"<Assignment Number>\"\nTax Reporting Unit: \"<Tax Reporting Unit>\"\nEffective Start Date: \"<Effective Start Date>\"\nEffective End Date: \"<Effective End Date>\"\n\nIf no exceptions are found, return: \"No exception due to tax reporting unit changes.\" \n\n\n\n{{$context.$variables.llmSysPrompt}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
